Strikers lets two people play Machine Strike against each other online, each in their own copy of Horizon Forbidden West. You both start a normal Machine Strike challenge, and the game's opponent on your PC plays the other person's moves. You place your own machines and take your own turns.

[b]Back up your saves before you use Strikers.[/b] Strikers changes the game while it runs, and the game keeps saving as you play. Your saves are in Documents\Horizon Forbidden West Complete Edition. Copy that folder somewhere safe.

[size=4][b]You both need[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Windows 10 or 11.
[*]Horizon Forbidden West Complete Edition on Steam. One copy each.
[*]The same game build. If they differ, Strikers tells you and will not start. Update the game in Steam on both PCs.
[*]The same Strikers version. Use the same download on both PCs.
[*]Machine Strike's Beginner's Tutorial finished.
[*]A save that has reached Salma's Machine Strike table in Chainscrape.
[*]Regular Challenge unlocked at Salma's table. Every match is played on it, whatever board you pick. To unlock it, beat Beginner's Practice: Easy, Medium and Hard. Or close the challenge list, press Unlock challenges in Strikers' Settings, and open the list again. That unlock lasts until the game restarts.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Install[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Unzip Strikers.zip into its own folder, not the top of a drive.
[*]Run Strikers.exe. It installs nothing and changes no game file. To remove it, delete the folder.
[*]Windows warns about an unknown publisher, because the download is not signed. Press More info, then Run anyway.
[*]Strikers does not work with Windows Smart App Control on. If Windows blocks live-probe.exe, turn Smart App Control off.
[*]Your antivirus may flag live-probe.exe. It reads and writes the game's memory during a match.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Play[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*][b]Both, in the game:[/b] go to Chainscrape, talk to Salma, choose Machine Strike, then Challenges. Stay on the challenge list. Do not enter a challenge yet.
[*][b]Both:[/b] run Strikers.exe. One of you hosts, the other joins.
[*][b]Host:[/b] under Host, pick the board, the points to win, the max army cost and who goes first. Press Create lobby. When the invite appears, press Copy and send it to the other player privately. Anyone with the invite can join the lobby.
[*][b]Joiner:[/b] under Join, press Paste, then Join. The board, the points and the cost come with the invite.
[*][b]Both:[/b] pick an army and press Use this army. Once the host has picked, the joiner can also pick Opponent's army for a mirror match. Build your army in the Armies panel before you create or join a lobby, because you cannot reach the panel after that.
[*][b]Both:[/b] a safety code appears. Read your four orange characters to the other player. Type the four they read to you into the box under the code. Press Codes match, continue. If the codes do not match, or no code appears, stop and start again. The code is not a secret. Only the invite must stay private.
[*][b]Both:[/b] with the game on the challenge list, press Set up the match. This takes about half a minute.
[*][b]Both:[/b] wait for the green message You are both ready. Enter the challenge now. Entering before it makes the boards stop matching. You then have ten minutes to enter, and a countdown shows the time left.
[*][b]Both:[/b] enter Regular Challenge and place your machines, taking turns. Do not back out of the challenge list on the way in.
[*][b]Play.[/b] Take your turn and end it. Strikers sends it. The other player's turn plays out as the game's opponent. Nothing in Strikers needs pressing.
[/list]
Keep Strikers open on both PCs until the match ends. Closing it on either PC ends the match. When the match ends, press Continue in the game, then Stop in Strikers. To play again, start over from Create lobby.

[size=4][b]If something goes wrong[/b][/size]
When a match stops, Strikers saves a report zip in the reports folder beside Strikers.exe. Settings has a Save report button for any other time. To ask for help, open an issue at the source link at the bottom of this page and attach the report from both PCs.
[list]
[*][b]Stopped: the two games disagree.[/b] The boards no longer match. Press Stop and start a new match.
[*][b]Stopped: you left the match[/b] or [b]your opponent left the match.[/b] One of you quit the match in the game before it ended. Press Stop and start a new match.
[*][b]Your opponent stopped.[/b] They pressed Stop or closed Strikers. Press Stop and start again.
[*][b]Your opponent left.[/b] Strikers waits for them to come back. If they do not, press Stop and start again.
[*][b]Lost the connection.[/b] Strikers keeps trying for a moment. If it does not reconnect, press Stop on both PCs and start again.
[*][b]Could not reach your opponent[/b] after Join. The host closed Strikers, or the invite is from an older lobby. Ask for a new invite.
[*][b]That is not an invite.[/b] Paste the whole invite: an address with a port, a long room id and a six-character code.
[*][b]You and the other player have different versions of Strikers.[/b] The message says who is behind. That player downloads the newest zip and unzips it over their folder.
[*][b]Your games are on different builds.[/b] Update the game in Steam on both PCs, then try again.
[*][b]The game is still in a match, or on its victory screen.[/b] Press Continue in the game, go back to the challenge list, and press Set up the match again.
[*][b]Another Strikers is running a match.[/b] Only one match per PC. Use that window, or press Stop in it first.
[/list]

[size=4][b]What Strikers does on your PC[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]It never plays for you.
[*]It installs nothing and changes no game file.
[*]During a match it reads and writes the game's memory, and changes a few parts of the game's code so the game's opponent plays the other player's moves. It undoes the code changes when the match ends. Closing the game clears the rest.
[*]The other player never sees your IP address. Both PCs connect through the public tunnel at bore.pub, and everything in it is encrypted between the two of you.
[*]It offers to download a background picture and a window icon from files.catbox.moe. Both are images from the game. Say no and it looks plain.
[*]Each time it opens, it asks Nexus Mods for the newest version. It sends nothing about you or your games.
[/list]
This mod changes a single-player game on your own PC. The game's publisher does not support it.


Source code and issues: [url=https://github.com/everydayaussie/Strikers]https://github.com/everydayaussie/Strikers[/url]
